---
// src/pages/bucknell/index.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell
// For the Bucknell business analytics search (Analytics & Operations Management, Freeman College of Management).
// The page is Meow-Dle, the mock Moodle, and nothing else (Ali, 19 Nov 2026: "i think we should remove all the
// commentary and just leave Meow-Dle"): no title, no lede and no section heading above it. Meow-Dle's name, across
// the top of the shell, is the page's h1.
// Meow-Dle opens on the class Ali teaches on his campus visit (Ali, 17 Nov 2026: "For Bucknell, focus on building out
// a mock LMS around the one lesson that I am teaching"): ANOP 102, week 11, class 2, "Playlists or radio?"
// (MoodleShell.astro, content in src/data/bucknell102.ts, the regression in SongsDemo.astro). Bucknell set the topic:
// multiple linear regression, at the level of ANOP 102. The visit's 30 minutes, and what they cover (Bucknell asked
// for this; it was in the lede too until 19 Nov), are marked in the class plan.
// The lesson is his of 17 Nov 2026 (the same class runs at Tulane): the 150 top-ranked songs released from January
// 2023 to early June 2024 in the Kaggle dataset, gaps in the data left out, radio against playlists.
// Bucknell's orange (the section colour) marks where you are in Meow-Dle, what the sample student has done, the
// visit's 30 minutes and a rubric's best level.
// The course pages (/bucknell/anop-102/ and its pack, ANOP 302, 330 and 400) go with this page; ANOP 102's is linked
// from the shell's syllabus. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import MoodleShell from '../../components/MoodleShell.astro';
import { bucknellColours } from '../../data/bucknell';
---
<Base title="Bucknell" description="Playlists or radio? The multiple regression class Ali Rizvi teaches on his Bucknell campus visit, for ANOP 102, laid out in Meow-Dle, a mock Moodle." noindex accent={bucknellColours}>
  <MoodleShell start="mdl-class2" />
</Base>
